<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gleb Vseslavich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1119">1119</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gleb Vseslavich was the first prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minsk">Minsk</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vseslav-of-polotsk">Vseslav of Polotsk</a> who received the town on his father's death in 1101. He fought the princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-ii-monomakh">Vladimir Monomakh</a>, who captured him in 1119. He died in captivity in Kiev the same year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gleb-vseslavich.jpg" alt="Gleb Vseslavich" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Печать Глеба Всеславича · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Gleb_Vseslavich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
